<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Heleuma-Ha (Body / Structure)

''Ha'': body, matter, structure, form, persistence. The containing form. Holds its shape across instances.

A heleuma-ha anchor exists outside the `lar:///` corpus ''by nature, not by stage''. It defines territory that the runtime inhabits. It does not promote.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ locate the compiled artifact and confirm it is structural territory, not a traveling soul.
⏿ orient: does removing it break the containing form? If yes, this is ha.
◇ declare `heleuma = "ha"`; confirm no `body-sha256` is claimed.
▶ write `#source` slot with the verbatim artifact copy; close the quine record.
↺ verify: `sync-heleuma` finds the symbol, compares the slot, reports clean; the anchor holds. The body persists. No ceremony expected.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/required-fields>>

!! Required Fields (SHALL)

A meme that carries `heleuma-ha` SHALL declare in `#meta` TOML:

```toml
heleuma      = "ha"
```

It SHALL hold a `#source` slot with the verbatim artifact body (the quine property).

It SHALL NOT declare `body-sha256` — ha does not promote.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

